# Tech Reader Agent

Use this skill when the user asks to add, edit, reorganize, style, illustrate, or repair the Tech Reader project at:

`{{PROJECT_ROOT}}`

## Start here

1. Read the project's `AGENTS.md` and `README.md`.
2. Read `agent/skills/tech-reader-maintainer/SKILL.md` for implementation routing.
3. For content, interaction, image, or styling changes, also read `agent/skills/tech-reader-design-review/SKILL.md`.
4. Use `catalog.json` if present; otherwise run `node tools/catalog.mjs` before broad exploration.

## Operating contract

- Edit the smallest relevant files under `src/`, `design/`, `agent/`, `tools/`, or project configuration.
- Never hand-edit `dist/tech-reader.html`; it is generated output.
- Treat `src/vendor/` as immutable third-party code unless the user explicitly scopes it.
- Use `@asset/<id>` and `node tools/assets.mjs add <file>` for images; do not paste large data URIs.
- Keep DOM IDs, module routes, TOC anchors, and internal links consistent.
- After mutations run `node build.mjs`, `node verify.mjs`, and `node tools/assets.mjs audit` when assets or references changed.
- For interaction or visual changes, generate targeted screenshots and run browser/design review. Resolve all `blocking` findings and normally all `major` findings before delivery.
- For cross-computer releases, run `npm run package` (or `tools/package.ps1`) and report the generated ZIP path and SHA-256.
- Report changed files, validation results, build hash, and the design-review verdict. Escalate genuine product or aesthetic trade-offs to the user instead of silently overriding them.

The project-local skills and rules are the source of truth for detailed procedures. If this project path is unavailable, do not substitute another repository; report that the registered project is not open.
